{"beat": 1, "name": "COLD OPEN", "text": "Saturday, June 21, 1879. The circus has come to Lancaster, Pennsylvania, with its parade down the city streets, and a young man whose first store has already closed is opening another he can barely afford. The rent is $30 a month. The stock, $410 of it, is much of it on credit. He has 7 clerks, and he hasn't advertised. He spends the morning worrying whether anyone will come. Every item in the store costs the same: a nickel. By tea time they've taken $47.65. By closing, $127.65. That's 2,553 separate sales, at one price, and 31% of everything in the store gone in a day. The next morning he wrote to his father: We could have sold $200 if the store had been larger.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "Saturday,", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.38}, {"word": "June", "start": 0.6, "end": 0.82}, {"word": "21,", "start": 0.82, "end": 1.4}, {"word": "1879.", "start": 1.76, "end": 3.4}, {"word": "The", "start": 4.22, "end": 4.32}, {"word": "circus", "start": 4.32, "end": 4.6}, {"word": "has", "start": 4.6, "end": 4.84}, {"word": "come", "start": 4.84, "end": 5.08}, {"word": "to", "start": 5.08, "end": 5.24}, {"word": "Lancaster,", "start": 5.24, "end": 5.9}, {"word": "Pennsylvania,", "start": 6.22, "end": 6.68}, {"word": "with", "start": 7.06, "end": 7.16}, {"word": "its", "start": 7.16, "end": 7.3}, {"word": "parade", "start": 7.3, "end": 7.64}, {"word": "down", "start": 7.64, "end": 7.9}, {"word": "the", "start": 7.9, "end": 8.08}, {"word": "city", "start": 8.08, "end": 8.22}, {"word": "streets,", "start": 8.22, "end": 8.64}, {"word": "and", "start": 8.94, "end": 9.14}, {"word": "a", "start": 9.14, "end": 9.26}, {"word": "young", "start": 9.26, "end": 9.38}, {"word": "man", "start": 9.38, "end": 9.66}, {"word": "whose", "start": 9.66, "end": 9.88}, {"word": "first", "start": 9.88, "end": 10.2}, {"word": "store", "start": 10.2, "end": 10.56}, {"word": "has", "start": 10.56, "end": 10.74}, {"word": "already", "start": 10.74, "en